{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/skiplists"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"title":"SkipLists","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","externalID":"SkipLists","modules":[{"name":"SkipLists"}]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is a sorted set kept in a skip list (Pugh, 1990): sorted linked lists stacked in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"levels, each level a random sample of the one below, searched from the top level down. Each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element’s tower gains a level with probability 1\/4, so lookup, insertion and removal take","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(log ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") expected time with no rebalancing. Its elements are a random-access collection in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ascending order, indexed by rank, with ","type":"text"},{"code":"lowerBound(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"upperBound(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"elements(in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":";","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the API matches the sorted sets of ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinarySearchTrees","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SkipLists","","var numbers: SkipList = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","numbers.insert(4)","numbers.contains(2)     \/\/ false","numbers.lowerBound(5)   \/\/ 3, the index of 5"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tower heights come from a random number generator given at creation; a seeded one makes every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list reproducible. The list’s levels are a directed acyclic graph, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList\/layersView-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" exposes to Grafluent’s algorithms and drawings as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(import Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"GraphProtocols","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" module beside this one): a vertex for each element on each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level of its tower, an edge along each level and an edge down each tower.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Skip lists as sorted sets, with their levels as a directed graph."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Sorted sets","anchor":"Sorted-sets","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList"]}],"references":{"doc://SkipLists/documentation/SkipLists/SkipList":{"url":"\/documentation\/skiplists\/skiplist","title":"SkipList","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SkipList","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SkipList","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A sorted set kept in a skip list: sorted linked lists stacked in levels, each level a random"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sample of the one below, searched from the top level down (Pugh, 1990)."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SkipLists/documentation/SkipLists/SkipList/layersView-swift.property":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"layersView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SkipList","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:9SkipLists0A4ListV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"text":"LayersView","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:9SkipLists0A4ListVAASHRzrlE10LayersViewV"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList\/layersView-swift.property","abstract":[{"text":"The list’s levels as a directed graph: a vertex for each element on each level of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tower, an edge from each to the next element on the same level, and an edge from each down","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the same element on the level below. The head is not a vertex.","type":"text"}],"conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}]},"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/skiplists\/skiplist\/layersview-swift.property","type":"topic","title":"layersView"},"doc://SkipLists/documentation/SkipLists":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Skip lists as sorted sets, with their levels as a directed graph."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists","url":"\/documentation\/skiplists","kind":"symbol","title":"SkipLists"}}}